<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ypres</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Ieper</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ypres (Ieper) is a city in West <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/flanders">Flanders</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a>. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> it was one of the three great cloth towns of the County of Flanders, with a vast Cloth Hall, and one of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/four-members-of-flanders">Four Members of Flanders</a>. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a> it lay at the centre of a salient that saw some of the war's heaviest fighting; the town was destroyed and rebuilt, and the Menin Gate commemorates the missing.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ypres.jpg" alt="Ypres" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Marc Ryckaert · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ieper_Grote_Markt_R04.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
